{"title":"Half-open interval","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>A <b>half-open interval</b> is an <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Interval\" title=\"Interval\">interval</a> which has either a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Maximum\" title=\"Maximum\">maximum</a> or a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Minimum\" title=\"Minimum\">minimum</a> element but not both. \n</p><p>If a half-open interval has a minimum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> but no maximum, then it is denoted by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/0/2905fb4cb148b1dc66f2cf1b1b0cee4353a594af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Least_upper_bound\" title=\"Least upper bound\">supremum</a> (least upper bound), or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/7/b671f1bb7e4ee86584347d5d22f1dc8abdb5bef2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\infty$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"9\" /> if no supremum exists. Alternatively, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/0/2905fb4cb148b1dc66f2cf1b1b0cee4353a594af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Set\" title=\"Set\">set</a> of all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/5/7c58301adca2a9f1f544c8ac00483fbff9177ca9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\leq x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/7/f87bae4e1be45e1aa97a25f6ffca964dd954e3c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &lt; b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />. \n</p><p>If a half-open interval has a maximum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> but no minimum, then it is denoted by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/f/cdf3085063293f29962808ba253dec1faa9866fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"20\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Greatest_lower_bound\" title=\"Greatest lower bound\">infimum</a> (greatest lower bound), or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/a/afac538740054d4786c170ef0123850adea5cdf9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\infty$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" /> if no infimum exists. Alternatively, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/f/cdf3085063293f29962808ba253dec1faa9866fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"20\" /> is the set of all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/e/dee577de87a897fba96ff88108acd587b2409030.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &lt; x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/9/9091d1105fa5758421a308f59fc695a5a209df1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\leq b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Examples\">Examples</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Half-open_interval&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Examples\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/e/89ef1891d5d450a742b18ae0767db38f5db90e52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[-1,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" /> is a half-open interval with a minimum but no maximum.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/4/e147ba06933a19883fc3a01f29328f188b9f6fdb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-1,1]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" /> is a half-open interval with a maximum but no minimum.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/d/ded3bde3015916b491ef54f95c4be9ff5c27ce63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0,\\infty)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"49\" height=\"20\" />, the set of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Nonnegative\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Nonnegative\">nonnegative</a> real numbers, is a half-open interval with no supremum.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/d/50d25d3e486146edd225ea505aaa53016f41edb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-\\infty,0]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" />, the set of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Nonpositive\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Nonpositive\">nonpositive</a> real numbers, is a half-open interval with no infimum.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Half-open_interval&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Open_interval\" title=\"Open interval\">Open interval</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Closed_interval\" title=\"Closed interval\">Closed interval</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Half-open_interval&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017174841\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.017 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.027 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 120/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 295/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3501/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.646      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.646      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:22565:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017174841 and revision id 172343. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}